Z||000003||coyote||05-03-2000||11:42 AM||||you might want to check the copper traces on the pod side of the connectors, they really do not like to be moved around a lot, sometimes they build up a corrosion and need to be cleaned. Sometimes they break.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||05-03-2000||12:22 PM||||If you had the instrument cluster out, did you remember to plug all three connectors back in? Two in the back (left and right sides) and one that plugs in from the bottom on the left side (driver side).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-03-2000||01:00 PM||||Also as BatBoy says if the connector that plugs in the back wasn't locked in it could have loosened. Does all the gages themselves still work?||||reg||1
